  "content": {
    "problemStatement": "Given an integer array AAA, print all possible **non-empty** subsets of AAA.\n\n\nInput Format\n\nThe first line of input will contain a single integer TTT, denoting the number of test cases.\nEach test case consists of two lines of input.\n\nThe first line of each test case contains two integers NNN - size of array AAA.\nThe second line contains NNN space-separated integers - the array AAA.\n\n\n\n\nOutput Format\nFor each test case, output M+1M+1M+1 lines, where MMM is the number of subsets:\n\n\n\nThe first line contains a single integer MMM.\nThe next MMM lines contains a subset of AAA.\n\nNote:\n\n\n\nElements in the subset must be in non-decreasing order.\nSubsets must not be duplicated.\nThe subsets must be sorted lexicographically. Subset XXX is said to be lexicographically smaller than subset YYY if either XXX is a prefix of YYY or there exists an index iii such that for all j&lt;ij \\lt ij&lt;i, Xj=YjX_j = Y_jXj​=Yj​ and Xi&lt;YiX_i \\lt Y_iXi​&lt;Yi​.",
    "constraints": [
      "1≤T≤101 \\leq T \\leq 101≤T≤10",
      "1≤N≤201 \\leq N \\leq 201≤N≤20",
      "1≤Ai≤1001 \\leq A_i \\leq 1001≤Ai​≤100",
      "The sum of NNN over all test cases won't exceed 303030."
    ],
    "inputFormat": "",
    "outputFormat": "",
    "notes": [],
    "sampleTestCases": [
      {
        "id": "sample_1",
        "type": "reg",
        "input": "3\n1\n1\n3\n1 2 2\n3\n1 2 3",
        "output": "1\n1 \n5\n1 \n1 2 \n1 2 2 \n2 \n2 2 \n7\n1 \n1 2 \n1 2 3 \n1 3 \n2 \n2 3 \n3",
        "explanation": "Explanation:\nTest case 111: Given AAA as [1][1][1].\nThere is only 111 non-empty subset of AAA which is{[1]}\\{[1]\\}{[1]}.\nTest case 222: Given AAA as [1,2,2][1, 2, 2][1,2,2].\nThere are 555 different non-empty subsets which are {[1],[1,2],[1,2,2],[2],[2,2]}\\{[1], [1, 2], [1, 2, 2], [2], [2, 2]\\}{[1],[1,2],[1,2,2],[2],[2,2]}.\nTest case 333: Given AAA as [1,2,3][1, 2, 3][1,2,3].\nThere are 777 different non-empty subsets which are {[1],[1,2],[1,2,3],[1,3],[2],[2,3],[3]}\\{[1], [1, 2], [1, 2, 3], [1, 3], [2], [2, 3], [3]\\}{[1],[1,2],[1,2,3],[1,3],[2],[2,3],[3]}."
      }
    ]
  },
